## Advanced REST paths with subdirectories

Note

The Data API builder functionality described in this section is available in version 2.0 and later. For more information, see [What's new in version 2.0](/en-us/azure/data-api-builder/whats-new/version-2-0).

Entity REST paths can include forward slashes to create subdirectory-style URL segments. This configuration enables more expressive, hierarchical URL structures for your API.

Configure a subdirectory path in the entity's `rest.path` property:

```
{
  "entities": {
    "ShoppingCartItem": {
      "source": "dbo.ShoppingCartItem",
      "rest": {
        "path": "shopping-cart/item"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

This configuration results in the endpoint:

```
GET /api/shopping-cart/item
```

DAB uses longest-prefix matching for routing, so more specific paths are matched before shorter ones. For security, validation blocks path traversal patterns (such as `..`), backslashes, and percent-encoded separators.

For more information, see the [REST path configuration](../../configuration/entities#rest-entity-name-entities).

